xt{mod}\\,2)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10a & ≡10b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\ 2\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5) \\\\ 5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(5,2)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3822141e-3cea-5c34-b925-a522c2273335" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Division Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26bee83a-d0b0-540d-abf4-27c985c7467f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414942} {:answer/id #uuid "6d525025-b858-597d-81f2-ca5669d4e790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414963} {:answer/id #uuid "b21f5aff-6f4d-5471-a3b6-6cc217f29b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414991} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d8562b-f70b-5c3a-